---
module: catalog
context: Catalogue
target: java
---

# Product Catalogue

Products and the prices Sales quotes them at. This context is upstream of Sales,
which reaches it through an anti-corruption layer.

## value object Price
- amount: decimal, required, min 0
- currency: text, required, length 3

## aggregate Product
identified by id

- id: uuid, required
- sku: text, required, unique, min length 3
- name: text, required, max length 200
- price: Price, required
- active: boolean, required, default true

invariant "an inactive product cannot be sold at zero price":
  active is false or price.amount is greater than 0

operation deactivate () -> nothing:
  set active to false

## error ProductNotFound (checked, status 404)
message: "no product exists with id {productId}"

- productId: uuid, required

## port ProductRepository (outbound)
using sql
config:
  table = products

- find product by id (id: uuid) -> Product or ProductNotFound
- save product (product: Product) -> nothing

## port CatalogueQueries (inbound)
- read product (id: uuid) -> Product or ProductNotFound

## service CatalogueService
uses ProductRepository
implements CatalogueQueries

operation read product (id: uuid) -> Product or ProductNotFound:
  let product be find product by id with id = id
  return product

## endpoint GET /products/{id}
handled by CatalogueService.read product
responds 200 with Product
responds 404 when ProductNotFound

## infrastructure
port 8081
database catalogdb using postgres version 16
deploy to docker, kubernetes
